        "x1": 413.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Choose a word from the text in A opposite to answer the questions."
      },
      {
        "y": 88,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 536.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "1 What is the early 20th century school of art which shows unusual or impossible things happening?"
      },
      {
        "y": 100,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 472,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "2 What is the mid 20th century school of art which has its origins in optical illusions?"
      },
      {
        "y": 112,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 530.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "3 What is the early 20th century school of art which depicts people or objects as a set of geometric"
      },
      {
        "y": 124,
        "x0": 127.6,
        "x1": 161.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "shapes?"
      },
      {
        "y": 136,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 512.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "4 What is the late 19th century school of art whose aim was to represent the effects of light on"
      },
      {
        "y": 148,
        "x0": 127.6,
        "x1": 202.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "people or scenes?"
      },
      {
        "y": 160,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 462.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "5 What phrase can be used to mean the content of a painting or other work of art?"
      },
      {
        "y": 172,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 489.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "6 What phrase can be used to describe someone with an educated understanding of art?"
      },
      {
        "y": 188.3,
        "x0": 78.5,
        "x1": 102,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "21.2"
      },
      {
        "y": 190.9,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 321,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Read the sentences and answer the questions."
      },
      {
        "y": 207.3,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 343.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "1 Finn enjoys painting but he’s a dauber not an artist."
      },
      {
        "y": 219.3,
        "x0": 127.6,
        "x1": 377.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Does the speaker have a high or low opinion of Finn’s work?"
      },
      {
        "y": 231.3,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 438.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "2 Curious as it now seems, the artist’s work was deemed morally dangerous."
      },
      {
        "y": 243.3,
        "x0": 127.6,
        "x1": 419,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Is this sentence more likely to come from a formal or informal source?"
      },
      {
        "y": 255.3,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 290,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "3 The sculptor is now inured to criticism."
      },
      {
        "y": 267.3,
        "x0": 127.6,
        "x1": 299.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "How is the sculptor affected by criticism?"
      },
      {
        "y": 279.3,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 467.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "4 While at art school, Matilda was particularly interested in the Cubist school of art."
      },
      {
        "y": 291.3,
        "x0": 127.6,
        "x1": 377.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "What is the difference between art school and school of art?"
      },
      {
        "y": 307.7,
        "x0": 78.5,
        "x1": 102,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "21.3"
      },
      {
        "y": 310.2,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 430.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Look at the adjectives in B opposite. Divide them into these categories:"
      },
      {
        "y": 330.1,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 524.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "usually positive associations usually negative associations negative or positive associations"
      },
      {
        "y": 345.8,
        "x0": 78.5,
        "x1": 102,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "21.4"
      },
      {
        "y": 348.4,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 497.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Choose one of the words from each pair of opposites in B and think of a work of art (of"
      },
      {
        "y": 360.4,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 465.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "any kind) that you could apply it to. Write a sentence explaining why it applies."
      },
      {
        "y": 377.7,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 532.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "example I think that the paintings by Salvador Dali could be called intriguing, because he uses such curious and surprising images."
      },
      {
        "y": 393.2,
        "x0": 78.5,
        "x1": 102,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "21.5"
      },
      {
